WEBVTT

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.608
This repository is a bank front end

00:00:02.658 --> 00:00:04.256
with no bank behind it.

00:00:04.306 --> 00:00:05.187
Every account

00:00:05.237 --> 00:00:06.191
every transfer

00:00:06.241 --> 00:00:08.770
and every sign in is answered inside

00:00:08.820 --> 00:00:09.630
the browser.

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:12.138
It is a synthetic Angular workspace

00:00:12.188 --> 00:00:14.574
and its purpose is to be upgraded.

00:00:14.624 --> 00:00:17.010
The workspace has two applications

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:18.444
two shared libraries

00:00:18.494 --> 00:00:19.948
and no server at all.

00:00:20.950 --> 00:00:24.076
Start with what the workspace actually contains.

00:00:24.126 --> 00:00:26.921
Angular CLI defines four projects under one

00:00:26.971 --> 00:00:27.781
angular.json.

00:00:27.831 --> 00:00:29.964
digital-banking is the retail app

00:00:30.014 --> 00:00:32.942
and wealth-portal is a downstream team's app.

00:00:32.992 --> 00:00:35.853
ui and analytics-sdk are libraries that both

00:00:35.903 --> 00:00:37.176
applications import.

00:00:37.226 --> 00:00:39.757
The README states the code is synthetic

00:00:39.807 --> 00:00:41.477
so it is safe to break and

00:00:41.527 --> 00:00:42.006
rebuild.

00:00:43.050 --> 00:00:43.285
Next

00:00:43.335 --> 00:00:44.425
the build graph.

00:00:44.475 --> 00:00:47.632
Each library is packaged with ng-packagr into

00:00:47.682 --> 00:00:48.772
the dist folder.

00:00:48.822 --> 00:00:52.192
The applications import the libraries by package

00:00:52.242 --> 00:00:52.477
name

00:00:52.527 --> 00:00:53.688
not by file path.

00:00:53.738 --> 00:00:56.610
So the libraries must build before either

00:00:56.660 --> 00:00:57.536
app can start

00:00:57.586 --> 00:01:00.814
and the build:libs script enforces that order.

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.703
Getting the workspace running takes three commands.

00:01:05.753 --> 00:01:08.993
First npm ci installs the pinned dependency

00:01:09.043 --> 00:01:09.299
tree

00:01:09.349 --> 00:01:11.978
and it builds both libraries on the

00:01:12.028 --> 00:01:12.284
way.

00:01:12.334 --> 00:01:15.039
Then npm start serves the retail app

00:01:15.089 --> 00:01:16.034
on port 4200.

00:01:16.084 --> 00:01:19.324
The wealth portal serves separately on port

00:01:19.374 --> 00:01:21.697
4300 with npm run start:wealth.

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:25.212
Here is the part worth remembering.

00:01:25.262 --> 00:01:27.974
Every HTTP call walks one fixed chain

00:01:28.024 --> 00:01:29.168
of interceptors.

00:01:29.218 --> 00:01:31.930
AuthInterceptor adds a correlation id

00:01:31.980 --> 00:01:34.467
and a bearer token for non-SSO API

00:01:34.517 --> 00:01:34.915
calls.

00:01:34.965 --> 00:01:38.050
ErrorInterceptor turns a 401 into a logout

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:40.587
and a server failure into a toast.

00:01:40.637 --> 00:01:43.946
Then MockBackendInterceptor answers any /api/

00:01:43.996 --> 00:01:44.991
request itself

00:01:45.041 --> 00:01:47.155
with a 250 millisecond delay.

00:01:47.205 --> 00:01:50.290
Because the mock sits before the analytics

00:01:50.340 --> 00:01:51.633
timing interceptor

00:01:51.683 --> 00:01:54.694
mocked calls never produce timing events.

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:58.331
Sign in follows the same two-step shape

00:01:58.381 --> 00:01:59.872
a real bank would use.

00:01:59.922 --> 00:02:02.043
The app posts the online id and

00:02:02.093 --> 00:02:04.144
passcode to /api/sso/authorize

00:02:04.194 --> 00:02:07.155
and keeps the returned challenge in memory.

00:02:07.205 --> 00:02:10.167
A one-time code goes to /api/sso/mfa/verify

00:02:10.217 --> 00:02:12.548
and the session token is stored in

00:02:12.598 --> 00:02:13.598
sessionStorage.

00:02:13.648 --> 00:02:16.049
Tokens expire after fifteen minutes

00:02:16.099 --> 00:02:18.290
and the next call with no bearer

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.551
logs the user out.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:22.795
Four retail features sit on top of

00:02:22.845 --> 00:02:23.470
that core.

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.440
The dashboard shows accounts and third-party

00:02:26.490 --> 00:02:27.453
provider cards.

00:02:27.503 --> 00:02:30.423
Accounts lists transactions for one account.

00:02:30.473 --> 00:02:32.448
Transfers validates the amount

00:02:32.498 --> 00:02:34.473
then updates the mock balance.

00:02:34.523 --> 00:02:36.566
Bill pay sends a payment record

00:02:36.616 --> 00:02:39.469
and deliberately leaves balances untouched.

00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.669
The mock backend is where all the

00:02:42.719 --> 00:02:43.425
data lives.

00:02:43.475 --> 00:02:45.212
It is a single interceptor

00:02:45.262 --> 00:02:47.962
about one hundred and thirty lines long.

00:02:48.012 --> 00:02:49.750
It matches exact API paths

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.637
and returns typed fixtures from the models

00:02:52.687 --> 00:02:52.981
file.

00:02:53.031 --> 00:02:55.594
It also holds the demo credentials and

00:02:55.644 --> 00:02:57.794
the fifteen minute token expiry.

00:02:57.844 --> 00:03:00.819
Production builds keep this mock switched on

00:03:00.869 --> 00:03:01.437
by design

00:03:01.487 --> 00:03:03.500
which the security page flags.

00:03:04.450 --> 00:03:08.063
Two libraries are shared between the applications.

00:03:08.113 --> 00:03:11.580
The ui library exports DbsUiModule: page headers

00:03:11.630 --> 00:03:12.532
account tiles

00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:13.485
alert banners

00:03:13.535 --> 00:03:14.583
a toast service

00:03:14.633 --> 00:03:17.441
and two pipes for currency and masking.

00:03:17.491 --> 00:03:20.518
Its theme mixin and a self-hosted Material

00:03:20.568 --> 00:03:23.009
Icons font are what keep both apps

00:03:23.059 --> 00:03:24.254
looking the same.

00:03:24.304 --> 00:03:27.111
The analytics SDK is the second library

00:03:27.161 --> 00:03:29.163
and it is the one that talks

00:03:29.213 --> 00:03:30.042
about users.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:34.100
The analytics SDK records four event types:

00:03:34.150 --> 00:03:34.749
page view

00:03:34.799 --> 00:03:35.542
interaction

00:03:35.592 --> 00:03:36.262
API timing

00:03:36.312 --> 00:03:36.983
and error.

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:40.011
Tracked clicks use an anTrack attribute in

00:03:40.061 --> 00:03:40.876
the template

00:03:40.926 --> 00:03:43.255
and outcomes call track directly.

00:03:43.305 --> 00:03:45.057
Before an event is queued

00:03:45.107 --> 00:03:48.157
scrub rewrites sensitive keys to the string

00:03:48.207 --> 00:03:48.806
REDACTED.

00:03:48.856 --> 00:03:51.545
The queue flushes every ten seconds to

00:03:51.595 --> 00:03:53.203
the analytics endpoint.

00:03:54.250 --> 00:03:56.956
Now the risk that shapes this repository.

00:03:57.006 --> 00:03:59.510
Five files under core carry a security

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:00.518
reviewed header

00:04:00.568 --> 00:04:03.073
and behaviour changes there need a new

00:04:03.123 --> 00:04:04.014
AppSec review.

00:04:04.064 --> 00:04:06.904
A vendor tarball pins Angular below fifteen

00:04:06.954 --> 00:04:09.391
so the first upgrade step cannot even

00:04:09.441 --> 00:04:09.660
run.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.550
Documented gates list the decisions a human

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.290
has to make

00:04:13.340 --> 00:04:15.508
instead of letting an agent pick.

00:04:16.550 --> 00:04:17.899
The numbers are small

00:04:17.949 --> 00:04:19.432
and that is deliberate.

00:04:19.482 --> 00:04:22.231
One hundred and fifteen tracked files hold

00:04:22.281 --> 00:04:24.430
about thirty three hundred lines.

00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.629
Fifty two TypeScript source files

00:04:26.679 --> 00:04:29.428
and seven spec files with seventeen tests.

00:04:29.478 --> 00:04:32.360
Both commits in the history were co-authored

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:33.026
by droids.

00:04:33.076 --> 00:04:35.758
Seven spec files against fifty two source

00:04:35.808 --> 00:04:38.091
files is a ratio worth remembering.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:39.813
So: install

00:04:39.863 --> 00:04:40.183
serve

00:04:40.233 --> 00:04:42.622
sign in with the demo credentials

00:04:42.672 --> 00:04:44.765
and follow the request chain.

00:04:44.815 --> 00:04:47.574
The pages behind this video cover each

00:04:47.624 --> 00:04:48.239
subsystem

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:49.496
the upgrade gates

00:04:49.546 --> 00:04:51.639
and the pitfalls already hit.

00:04:51.689 --> 00:04:53.339
Start with the overview

00:04:53.389 --> 00:04:56.074
then read the gates before you change

00:04:56.124 --> 00:04:56.739
anything.
